.TH COMPUST 1 2026-11-14 Compust "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
compust \- experimental X11 compositor for Xorg and XLibre
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compust
.RB [ \-\-display
.IR display ]
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR file ]
.br
.B compust
.RB [ \-\-display
.IR display ]
.B \-\-diagnose
.br
.B compust
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR file ]
.B \-\-check\-config
.br
.B compust
.BR \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B compust
composites the windows of one X screen.
It redirects them off screen through the Composite extension and draws each
frame from their contents, with fades when windows open and close,
transparency, blur behind translucent windows, shadows, rounded corners, and
settings chosen per window by rules.
It repaints only the regions that changed, and an idle desktop is not
repainted.
.PP
By default the X server draws the frames through XRender.
With
.B backend = \(dqgl\(dq
they are drawn with OpenGL ES on the server's GPU, sharing buffers through
DRI3, and Compust falls back to XRender with a warning where the server or
the driver cannot.
When the server supports Present, finished frames are presented in step with
the display; otherwise they are copied directly, which is not synchronized to
vertical blanking.
.PP
Compust becomes the compositor by owning the
.B _NET_WM_CM_S\fIn\fP
selection of the screen.
If another compositor owns it, Compust refuses to start and says so: stop
that compositor first.
Compust runs in the foreground until it is stopped, logs to standard error,
and installs no autostart entry.
Start it from the X session, after the window manager, for example with
.B spawnOnce \(dqcompust\(dq
in Xmonad or
.B exec \-\-no\-startup\-id compust
in i3.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-display " display"
Composite the screen of
.IR display ,
such as
.BR :1 ,
instead of the one that
.B DISPLAY
names.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIfile\fP"
Read the configuration from
.I file
instead of searching for it.
Saving
.I file
reloads it.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Report the server's extensions and whether blur and the GPU renderer can
run, without becoming the compositor.
It can run while another compositor is active.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration, print the file it was read from, or that
built-in defaults apply, and exit without connecting to the X server.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Without
.BR \-\-config ,
Compust reads the first
.I compust/compust.toml
in
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
(by default
.IR ~/.config ),
then in each directory of
.B $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
(by default
.IR /etc/xdg ).
Without a file, built-in defaults apply.
.BR compust.toml (5)
describes the settings.
An unknown setting or a value out of its range is an error, and Compust
exits before connecting to the X server.
.PP
Compust reloads the configuration without restarting when the file is saved,
once it has stayed unchanged for a tenth of a second, and on
.BR SIGUSR1 .
A reload reads the file that a restart would read.
If that file cannot be read or is invalid, Compust logs a warning and keeps
its current settings.
A configuration directory created after Compust starts is read on
.B SIGUSR1
or at the next start.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Reload the configuration.
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop compositing and exit.
The windows then draw to the screen directly again.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X display to composite, unless
.B \-\-display
names one.
The usual Xauthority authentication applies.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_DIRS ", " HOME
Where the configuration is searched for.
Relative directories are ignored.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Which messages are logged, by default
.BR compust=info ;
.B compust=debug
logs more.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/compust/compust.toml
The user's configuration, under the default
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/compust/compust.toml
A configuration for every user, under the default
.BR XDG_CONFIG_DIRS .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/compust/compust.example.toml
A complete example configuration, where packages install it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Compust was stopped by
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM ,
or
.B \-\-diagnose
or
.B \-\-check\-config
succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
An error, such as an invalid configuration, a missing extension, another
compositor owning the screen, or a lost connection to the server.
.TP
.B 2
An invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the server and the configuration, then start Compust with its log in
a file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
compust \-\-diagnose
compust \-\-check\-config
compust 2>>"$HOME/.local/state/compust.log" &
.EE
.RE
.PP
Reload the configuration by signal, as a directory created after Compust
started requires, and start Compust with more log messages:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pkill \-USR1 \-x compust
RUST_LOG=compust=debug compust
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR compust.toml (5),
.BR xprop (1)
.PP
The README in
.IR /usr/share/doc/compust ,
and the documentation at
.UR https://github.com/hashdefault/compust
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report problems with the issue templates at
.UR https://github.com/hashdefault/compust/issues
.UE .
